This is work in progress by Rob Speer - I'm leaving notes to myself for what to fill in.

;ko'a, ko'e, ko'i, ko'o, ko'u, fo'a, fo'e, fo'i, fo'o, fo'u: Assignable pro-sumti. The referent of each word is undefined until it is assigned using ''goi''. (''Do we mention using the ko'a series without goi?'')

;vo'a, vo'e, vo'i, vo'o, vo'u: The x1, x2, x3, x4, or x5 of this bridi, respectively. These pro-sumti refer to the sumti filling a place of the ''outermost'' bridi. (More detail...)

;ri: The previous sumti. (''define "previous sumti"'')
;ra: A recent sumti, usually not the previous.
;ru: An earlier sumti (''how early''?)

;ti, ta, tu: demonstrative pronouns (''separate them, and describe usage with and without "pointing"'')